 r←Test_InstallAndLoad_065(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;dir;src;src2;dist;body;cfg;parms;zipfile
⍝ Load a package that has neither assets nor files.\
⍝ Such a package leaves nothing behind that anybody could need: `LoadPackages` deletes the temp
⍝ folder it was unpacked into, and `HOME` is empty. That is the documented behaviour, and the
⍝ counterpart of Test_InstallAndLoad_064.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 #.⎕EX TC.GetTatinRootSpace'#'
 dir←∆GetTempDir ⍬
 (src dist)←(⊂dir,'/'),¨'src' 'dist'
 src,←'/v0.1.0'
 src2←src,'/APLSource'
 F.MkDir src2 dist

 body←'r←Hello' 'r←''World'''
 (⊂body)F.NPUT src2,'/Test.aplf'

 cfg←TC.InitPackageConfig ⍬
 cfg.group←'Example'
 cfg.name←'NoFootprint'
 cfg.version←'0.1.0'
 cfg.source←'APLSource/'
 cfg.os_win←1
 TC.WritePackageConfigFile src cfg

 parms←TC.CreateBuildParms src
 parms.targetPath←dist
 zipfile←TC.BuildPackage parms
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≥≢zipfile

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 {}⎕SE.Tatin.LoadPackages zipfile'#.TEMP'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢#.TEMP.NoFootprint.TatinVars.HOME

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 Assert 0=⊃F.RmDir dir
 #.⎕EX TC.GetTatinRootSpace'#'
⍝Done
